{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1396915-v20-miami-by-night-the-miami-food-chain","id":1396915,"title":"[V20] Miami by Night: The Miami Food Chain","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-16T12:13:40-07:00","id":1396915,"title":"[V20] Miami by Night: The Miami Food Chain","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/317465/Miami-by-Night-The-Miami-Food-Chain\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/images/1/317465.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/317465/Miami-by-Night-The-Miami-Food-Chain\" target=\"_blank\"> Miami by Night: The Miami Food Chain - White Wolf | Storytellers Vault </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/317465/Miami-by-Night-The-Miami-Food-Chain\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/317465/Miami-by-Night-The-Miami-Food-Chain </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Miami by Night: The Miami Food Chain - For most Cainites, the Sabbat is synonymous with the grit and violence of Detroit, the backstabbing politics of Mexico C </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I just released this on the Storytellers Vault, my first fan-made supplement EVER! It describes the various Sabbat packs (and others) residing in Miami and is designed to be used with VtM 3rd edition or V20. At 119 pages, I think it\u2019s worth $10! As you can see, I also did my best to make it look like one of the authentic VtM sourcebooks! There is something for Storytellers and players alike in here!<br /> <br /> I started this project in 2018 planning to write an entire Miami by Night sourcebook but just writing the character section was so overwhelming it took a global pandemic and quarantine to finish it. Please note that I am just one man working without an editor so there are typos and some minor mistakes in there, but I will be releasing an updated version very soon that fixes these.<br /> <br /> Description: For most Cainites, the Sabbat is synonymous with the grit and violence of Detroit, the backstabbing politics of Mexico City, or the darkly spiritual setting of Montreal. There is another Sabbat city, a bridge between North and South America, once the staging ground of Crusades against the Camarilla, now a debauched Babylon and Cathari paradise. Miami may be where neon goes to die, but it is also where the unliving go to lose themselves in mindless debauchery and wanton violence.<br /> <br /> These pages describe the various Sabbat packs (and others) who either reside in the city or have made it their home as they pursue their insidious agendas. Storytellers can either use these characters as NPCs in a campaign set in Miami or easily adapt them for their use in their own campaigns. Players can also use these characters for inspiration in crafting their own characters or in designing allies, contacts, or mentors for their Sabbat chronicles. There are also numerous storylines presented that describe relations between the packs, providing opportunities for political intrigue, social machinations, or straight-up no-holds-barred combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I am a prophet. I bring chaos and unrest to the foolish and wicked. I am no fit prince for Cainites, and I am no fit shepherd for the souls of men.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24720-anatole","name":"Anatole","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24720_2.png","title":"Member",